    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "# Problem\n\nTo support platforms not supported by LuaJIT, such as wasm, nvim keeps its codebase compatible with PUC Lua 5.1, and therefore cannot use some of the extended syntax provided by LuaJIT.\n\n# Expected behavior\n\nBy incorporating [lua-compat-5.3](https://github.com/lunarmodules/lua-compat-5.3) into the PUC Lua 5.1 build, we can enable support for certain LuaJIT extensions within the PUC Lua build. As shown below:\n\n## Lua APIs\nFeature | LuaJIT support | Lua 5.1 + compat53\n-- | -- | --\nload(chunk, name, mode, env) | Yes | Yes\nloadfile(filename, mode, env) | Yes | Yes\nloadstring() as alias/near-alias of load() | Yes | Mostly via load\nmath.log(x, base) | Yes | Yes\nstring.rep(s, n, sep) | Yes | Yes\nstring.format(\"%s\", x) calls tostring(x) | Yes | Yes\nxpcall(f, msgh, ...) passes extra args | Yes | Yes\npcall / xpcall can run yielding functions | Yes | Yes, with caveats\ntable.pack(...) | Yes | Yes\ntable.unpack(...) | Yes | Yes\ntable.move(a1, f, e, t, a2) | Yes | Yes\nrawlen(x) | Yes | Yes, but #table still differs\npackage.searchpath(...) | Yes | Yes\npackage.searchers | Yes | Yes, alias to package.loaders\npairs() respects __pairs | Yes, with LuaJIT 5.2 compat | Yes\ncoroutine.running() main-coroutine behavior | Yes | Partial / caveated\nio.write() returns file handle | Yes | Yes\nfile:write() returns file handle | Yes | Yes\nio.lines(...) accepts read formats | Yes | Yes\nfile:lines(...) accepts read formats | Yes | Yes\nos.execute() detailed status | Yes | Yes\npipe:close() / file:close() detailed status for io.popen | Yes | Yes\ndebug.setmetatable(x, mt) returns x | Yes | Yes\ndebug.getuservalue(u) | Yes | Yes\ndebug.setuservalue(u, v) | Yes | Yes\nassert(false, non_string_error) | Yes | Yes\n\n## C APIs\nC API feature | LuaJIT support | Lua 5.1 + compat53\n-- | -- | --\nlua_copy | Yes | Yes\nlua_absindex | Yes | Yes\nlua_compare | Yes | Yes\nlua_len | Yes | Yes\nlua_rawlen | Yes | Yes\nluaL_len | Yes | Yes\nlua_load / load with mode | Yes | Yes\nluaL_loadfilex | Yes | Yes\nluaL_loadbufferx | Yes | Yes\nluaL_fileresult | Yes | Yes\nluaL_execresult | Yes | Yes\nluaL_traceback | Yes | Yes\nluaL_setfuncs | Yes | Yes\nluaL_newlibtable | Yes | Yes\nluaL_newlib | Yes | Yes\nluaL_testudata | Yes | Yes\nluaL_setmetatable | Yes | Yes\n\n(Summarized using ChatGPT)",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
