            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I'd like to take this on. Plan:\n\n  lua-compat-5.3 v0.13 is already vendored (cmake.deps/deps.txt) but only wired into the luv build. I'll reuse\n  that same dep and compile compat-5.3.c into nvim core on the PUC Lua path:\n\n  - CMake: extend the PREFER_LUA block in src/nvim/CMakeLists.txt to add the compat53 source + include dir\n  (mirroring the existing bit.c / NVIM_VENDOR_BIT precedent), and ensure the lua_compat53 download target is\n  available to the core build, not just luv.\n  - Zig: mirror the same in src/build_lua.zig for the use_luajit == false path.\n\n  I'll verify with a -DPREFER_LUA=ON -DUSE_BUNDLED_LUA=ON build that the backported APIs (table.pack/move, rawlen,\n  package.searchpath, etc.) resolve, and keep both the LuaJIT and PUC configs green on functionaltest.\n  Simplifying the existing #if LUA_VERSION_NUM guards in bit.c/lua_cjson.c/lmpack.c would be a follow-up.\n\n  Does this approach sound right before I open a PR?\n(Summarized using Claude)",
